snapclientmpris (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Publish the real playback position: Position is what the stream's
    source reports through snapserver, advanced while playing, instead
    of a constant 0. A report that is not where playback was expected
    emits Seeked. MPRIS clients that trust CanSeek no longer show a
    position stuck at zero.
  * Forward Seek and SetPosition to the stream's source when it can
    seek. Both raised NotSupported before.
  * Publish mpris:trackid in Metadata, built from snapserver's trackId.

 -- Mathieu Réquillart <mathieu.requillart@gmail.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:39:08 +0200

snapclientmpris (1.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the bridge binding to a stale snapserver roster entry on hosts
    with several network interfaces up (for example wifi and ethernet):
    MPRIS showed another stream and volume changes had no effect. A
    connected entry is now preferred, and the bridge rebinds when one of
    its entries connects, disconnects, registers or is deleted from the
    server.

 -- Mathieu Réquillart <mathieu.requillart@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:28:26 +0200

